Subject: Quantum Computer Design

The ftp site for the quantum computer design recently mentioned in 
sci.nanotech is im.lcs.mit.edu:/poc/lloyd/lloyd.ps

"A Potentially Realizable Quantum Computer", Seth Lloyd, Center for 
Nonlinear Studies, LANL.

The abstract:

Arrays of weakly-coupled quantum systems can be made to compute by subjecting
them to a sequence of electromagnetic pulses of well-defined frequency and
length.  Such pulsed arrays are true quantum computers: bits can be placed
in superpostions of 0 and 1, logical operations take place coherently, and
dissipation is required only for error correction.  When operated at optical
frequencies, the array could provide massively parallel computation at 
clock cycles of nano- to pico-seconds.

